+## Session — 2026-10-08 (cont) — v1.264.0 (service kartu hadiah: Redeem menolak saldo kurang dan kartu kedaluwarsa)
+
+Scaffolded `service.GiftCardService.Redeem(ctx, code, amount)` at the user's request, service layer only: the repository, handler, router wiring, migration and the `gift_cards` table all still have to follow, so nothing reaches `Deps` or `/api` yet and the type is unreachable from the running binary. There was no gift-card or stored-value concept anywhere in the repo before this (grepped `gift` and `voucher` across Go and SQL: only `plan.go`'s unrelated wording and promo `kind`), so it extends nothing and duplicates nothing; the closest neighbour is `PromoService`, which discounts a cart from a coupon row rather than drawing down a stored balance, which is why this is its own service rather than a branch in that one. Refusals are sentinel `error` values in Indonesian because `writeError(…, err.Error(), …)` puts a service error string straight on the merchant's screen (`p-backend.md`): `ErrGiftCardCodeEmpty`, `ErrGiftCardNotFound`, `ErrGiftCardInactive`, `ErrGiftCardExpired`, `ErrGiftCardInsufficient`, `ErrGiftCardAmountInvalid`. The shape that matters is the write: `Redeem` pre-checks active/expiry/balance for a cheap, specific refusal, but the repository contract is a single conditional `Debit(id, amount, now) (bool, error)` whose WHERE repeats all three guards, because reading the balance in Go and writing it back lets two terminals redeeming the same card each pass the check and spend the balance twice. A zero-row debit therefore re-reads the row and re-derives the reason from the fresh copy rather than reporting the pre-race one, the same pattern `WriteOffReceivable` uses with `writeOffRefusal` and `finalizeSettle` with `ResolvePending`. Amount is BIGINT IDR and goes through `domain.ValidateBillAmount`, so a redeem that would net off a bill total beyond `MaxBillAmount` refuses instead of wrapping. The placeholder `GiftCard` struct and the `GiftCardRepository` interface sit in the service file for now and are flagged in-file to move to `internal/domain` / `internal/repository` with the migration. Verified: `go build ./...` clean, `go vet ./internal/service/` clean, and 14 cases in `gift_card_service_test.go` green against a fake repo whose `Debit` enforces the same guard, covering exact-balance, no-expiry, zero and negative amounts, expiry exactly at `now` (refused: `!now.Before(expiresAt)`), whitespace-only codes, code trimming and both mid-flight race arms. Falsified in both directions: deleting the expiry guard turned three cases red, deleting the balance guard turned two red through the assertion that a refusal never calls `Debit`, and the restored file is green again. Not committed and the server was never started, per the request. No changelog entry: there is no user-facing surface yet, and `docs/changelog.md` cannot be edited without `just docs-features` in the same commit.
+
+---
