 ## Session — 2026-10-08 (cont) — v1.264.0 (satu bentuk ID untuk SS/SUB/QTA/PF/PFI: awalan + YYYYMMDD + 4 angka)

 Before the first payout-ID change reached prod the user widened it: every reference KITAPOS or a merchant may type into a bank note becomes prefix + `YYYYMMDD` + four digits, no symbols, for SUB, QTA, SS (merchant payout, was `SP-`), PFI and PF; BILL, DP and PO stay as they are (user: "DP, PO, BILL biarin"). One owner now: `domain.NewReference(prefix, day)` / `FormatReference` in `internal/domain/reference.go` with the five `RefPrefix*` constants, replacing `subscriptionReference`, `quotaOrderReference`, `platformInvoiceCheckoutReference`, `PlatformFeeReference` (+ `platformReferenceSlugMax`) and the six-letter payout suffix from the previous entry, all deleted. Four random digits clash often enough to need a real path, so `repository.ErrReferenceTaken` (23505 on `<table>_reference_key`, matched by constraint name) drives a redraw up to `domain.ReferenceAttempts` (5) at every writer: SUB/QTA/PFI retry in the service around the reservation, SS retries its `ON CONFLICT (reference) DO NOTHING` insert, and PF retries inside the accrual transaction through a savepoint (`insertInvoiceRow`), because a failed statement would otherwise abort the caller's tx; an existing PF row takes the upsert's UPDATE branch, which never rewrites its reference. Found while wiring it: `quota_addon_repo.ReserveOrder` mapped ANY unique violation to `ErrPendingQuotaOrderExists`, so a reference clash would have read as "a pending order already exists"; the reference check now runs first. Migration 266 (append-only: 265 had already landed on dev) rewrites existing rows except those that reached a gateway (`redirect_url` or `gateway_trx_id` set), since a late payment arrives carrying the old ID; SS and PF were never sent to a gateway and are all rewritten. Measured on prod before writing it (read-only): SUB 10 rows, QTA 4, SS 2, PFI 0, PF 0; five SUB/QTA rows carry a gateway link (all internal or the user's own test) and keep their old IDs. Rehearsed in a rolled-back transaction on dev with prod-shaped rows (payout with and without report, DEMO SUB, Faspay-link SUB, SumoPod-trx SUB, link QTA, DEMO QTA, PF): every rule held and no eligible row was left in an old shape; applied to dev. Assertions moved: Hurl `hq/payout/01-history.hurl` `^SS20261005[0-9]{4}$`, `platform_invoices_hq_test.go` `^PFI[0-9]{12}$`, e2e `vendor/44` fixtures `SS2026100x….`. Capacity note: 10,000 IDs per prefix per day; SS issues one per merchant per Faspay report, so it is the first to feel it. Verified on isolated stacks: `just uat-fresh` over hq payout/platform-invoices/quota-addon/subscription 12/12 files, 170 requests (the three Mayar-only subscription slices cannot run under the stub provider); `just e2e-fresh` vendor/40, 41, 44 and 07-tagihan 16 passed. Not deployed: prod needs migrations 265 and 266.

